that we have a leadership
in machine learning.

00:37:20.730 --> 00:37:23.990
At Google Cloud we have
these pretrained machine

00:37:23.990 --> 00:37:26.400
learning APIs, which
allow you to easily do

00:37:26.400 --> 00:37:28.680
tasks such as use
computer vision

00:37:28.680 --> 00:37:31.590
to extract meaningful
information from images.

00:37:31.590 --> 00:37:33.210
Or use our Video
Intelligence API

00:37:33.210 --> 00:37:36.450
to be able to pull out metadata,
or meaningful information,

00:37:36.450 --> 00:37:38.220
from videos that
customers are trying

00:37:38.220 --> 00:37:41.059
to ingest into some
sort of object storage.

00:37:41.059 --> 00:37:42.600
We also released a
new service, known

00:37:42.600 --> 00:37:46.710
as AutoML, which is
riding off of the message

00:37:46.710 --> 00:37:49.860
from our CEO Sundar,
which is to democratize

00:37:49.860 --> 00:37:52.090
AI for the general public.

00:37:52.090 --> 00:37:54.420
And what democratized
AI means, is the fact

00:37:54.420 --> 00:37:58.660
that there is not as
many data scientists

00:37:58.660 --> 00:38:00.310
as are developers in the world.

00:38:00.310 --> 00:38:01.954
So being able to
empower developers

00:38:01.954 --> 00:38:03.370
with these machine
learning models

00:38:03.370 --> 00:38:05.950
that we've trained in-house
at Google, based off

00:38:05.950 --> 00:38:07.840
of running these data
sets through the data

00:38:07.840 --> 00:38:10.000
sets that we have running
our production systems,

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:13.600
and empowering these developers
with these black box APIs,

00:38:13.600 --> 00:38:15.430
that they can then
feed things into,

00:38:15.430 --> 00:38:18.570
to be able to drive
meaningful insights from.

00:38:18.570 --> 00:38:20.500
On the AutoML side,
we're basically

00:38:20.500 --> 00:38:23.200
making it so that you could
actually ingest and tweak

00:38:23.200 --> 00:38:26.530
these particular models to
meet more so to your data sets,

00:38:26.530 --> 00:38:28.950
and go through it easy
GUI to be able to train

00:38:28.950 --> 00:38:31.840
these models to meet
your tailored data sets.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:33.340
So to take this a
step further, what

00:38:33.340 --> 00:38:35.860
that means is that
the Vision API might

00:38:35.860 --> 00:38:39.700
be able to recognize that
this image is a dog or a cat.

00:38:39.700 --> 00:38:42.842
But then, if you were to train
this on a more deeper data

00:38:42.842 --> 00:38:44.770
set, which is something
that you as a customer

00:38:44.770 --> 00:38:47.530
brings to the table, you will
be able to actually recognize

00:38:47.530 --> 00:38:48.760
like a species of the dog.

00:38:48.760 --> 00:38:50.801
So maybe you will be able
to say this is not just

00:38:50.801 --> 00:38:52.430
a dog, but a golden retriever.

00:38:52.430 --> 00:38:54.631
Or this is not just a
dog, it is a poodle.

00:38:54.631 --> 00:38:56.380
So across the board,
doing a lot of things

00:38:56.380 --> 00:38:57.572
in machine learning space.

